    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Harden the Outlook add-in's auth + manifest last-mile (the `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy` foundation already ships on `master`, per Owner Clarification — no external blocker):

    1. **NAA migration** — migrate the add-in off the DEPRECATED `NaaAuthService` / `DialogAuthService` / `authConfig` onto the canonical `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`. Remove the deprecated services once no consumer remains. No self-bootstrapped MSAL; no `ConfidentialClientApplication`; token flows through `OfficeNaaStrategy` / `authenticatedFetch`.

    2. **Unified manifest** — the add-in currently has TWO mismatched manifests (XML v1.0.19 and JSON devPreview v1.0.0). Converge on the unified JSON manifest (the Microsoft-forward format), reconciling version + capabilities so a single manifest is the source of truth.

    3. **Org-URL fix** — replace the hardcoded org URL `spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com` with configuration (environment-tokenized), so the add-in is not pinned to the dev org.

    Build + deploy via the `office-addins-deploy` skill (Azure Static Web Apps / SWA CLI) and smoke-test the save flow in dev under NAA.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Office Add-ins engineer authoritative on the Outlook add-in shell, the `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy` (NAA / nested app auth), unified JSON manifest authoring, and the `office-addins-deploy` (SWA) pipeline. Familiar with ADR-028 Spaarke Auth v2.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The add-in authenticates exclusively via `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`; `NaaAuthService`/`DialogAuthService`/`authConfig` are removed. A single unified JSON manifest is the source of truth (versions reconciled). No hardcoded org URL remains (config-driven). The add-in builds and deploys via `office-addins-deploy`, and the save flow works end-to-end under NAA in dev.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per Owner Clarification, the auth foundation (`@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy` + BFF filter classes) is already on `master`; R4 owns the add-in's LAST-MILE wiring. The add-in still runs on deprecated auth services, carries two mismatched manifests, and pins the dev org URL. This is the client half of FR-25; task 073 applies the BFF Office endpoint filters, and task 074 surfaces engine suggestions in the save pane.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/shared/ (deprecated `NaaAuthService`/`DialogAuthService`/`authConfig`)</file>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/ (Outlook add-in shell + save task pane)</file>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/**/manifest*.xml (XML v1.0.19 — reconcile/retire)</file>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/**/manifest*.json (JSON devPreview v1.0.0 — unify onto this)</file>
      <file>@spaarke/auth `OfficeNaaStrategy` (canonical strategy on master)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-25">Migrate off `NaaAuthService`/`DialogAuthService`/`authConfig` onto `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`; converge on the unified JSON manifest; fix the hardcoded org URL; save flow works under NAA in dev.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client uses `@spaarke/auth` only (`OfficeNaaStrategy` for the add-in); MUST NOT `new` a credential or `ConfidentialClientApplication`; no token snapshots / `accessToken` props.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">No self-built credentials; central auth primitives only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Single manifest source of truth; do not leave two divergent manifests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Org URL config-driven / environment-tokenized — no `spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com` literal in shipped code.</constraint>
  </constraints>

